    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/725361",
      "sequence": 1,
      "source_sequence": 3310,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Centralizing Over-the-Counter Markets?",
      "title_cn": "集中化场外交易市场？",
      "authors": [
        "Jason Allen",
        "Milena Wittwer"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "In traditional over-the-counter markets, investors trade bilaterally through intermediaries. We assess whether and how to shift trades on a centralized platform with trade-level data on the Canadian government bond market. We document that intermediaries charge a markup when trading with investors and specify a model to quantify price and welfare effects from market centralization. We find that many investors would not use the platform, even if they could, because it is costly, competition for investors is low, and investors value relationships with intermediaries. Market centralization can even decrease welfare, unless competition is sufficiently strong.",
      "abstract_cn": "在传统的场外交易市场中，投资者通过中介机构进行双边交易。我们利用加拿大政府债券市场的交易层面数据，评估是否以及如何在集中化平台上转移交易。我们记录了中介机构在与投资者交易时收取加价，并构建了一个模型来量化市场集中化带来的价格和福利效应。我们发现，许多投资者即使可以使用该平台，也不会使用，因为成本高昂，投资者之间的竞争较低，且投资者重视与中介机构的关系。除非竞争足够激烈，否则市场集中化甚至可能降低福利。",
