    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/725171",
      "sequence": 2,
      "source_sequence": 3377,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Learning Efficiency of Multiagent Information Structures",
      "title_cn": "多智能体信息结构的学习效率",
      "authors": [
        "Mira Frick",
        "Ryota Iijima",
        "Yuhta Ishii"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "Which information structures are more effective at eliminating first- and higher-order uncertainty and hence at facilitating efficient play in coordination games? We consider a learning setting where players observe many private signals about the state. First, we characterize multiagent learning efficiency, that is, the rate at which players approximate common knowledge. We find that this coincides with the rate at which first-order uncertainty disappears, as higher-order uncertainty vanishes faster than first-order uncertainty. Second, we show that with enough signal draws, information structures with higher learning efficiency induce higher equilibrium welfare. We highlight information design implications for games in data-rich environments.",
      "abstract_cn": "哪些信息结构在消除一阶和高阶不确定性方面更有效，从而在协调博弈中促进有效博弈？我们考虑一个学习环境，其中玩家观察关于状态的许多私人信号。首先，我们刻画了多智能体学习效率，即玩家近似共同知识的速率。我们发现这与一阶不确定性消失的速率一致，因为高阶不确定性比一阶不确定性消失得更快。其次，我们表明，在足够的信号抽取下，具有更高学习效率的信息结构会带来更高的均衡福利。我们强调了数据丰富环境中博弈的信息设计启示。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1086/725171",
      "source_url": "https://doi.org/10.1086/725171",
