    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1086/725362",
      "sequence": 3,
      "source_sequence": 3497,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Multidimensional Sorting under Random Search",
      "title_cn": "随机搜索下的多维排序",
      "authors": [
        "Ilse Lindenlaub",
        "Fabien Postel-Vinay"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We analyze sorting in a frictional labor market when workers and jobs have multidimensional characteristics. We say that matching is positive assortative in dimension (j, k) if workers with higher endowment in skill k are matched to a job distribution with higher values of attribute j in the first-order stochastic dominance sense. Crucial for sorting is a single-crossing property of technology. Sorting is positive between worker-job attributes with strong complementarities but negative in other dimensions. Finally, sorting is based on comparative advantage: workers sort into jobs that suit their skill mix rather than their overall skill level.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们分析了当工人和工作具有多维特征时，摩擦性劳动力市场中的排序。我们说，如果技能k禀赋较高的工人按照一阶随机占优意义匹配到属性j值较高的工作分布，则匹配在维度(j, k)上是正分类匹配的。对排序至关重要是技术的单交叉性质。在工人-工作属性之间具有强互补性的维度上，排序是正的，但在其他维度上是负的。最后，排序基于比较优势：工人会进入适合其技能组合的工作，而不是其整体技能水平。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1086/725362",
